---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { NewTabLink } from '../components/NewTabLink';
import { encodeState } from '../components/state';
import { REPO_URL } from '../config';
import { HEADER_POLICY, META_DIRECTIVES } from '../site-policy';

const metaPolicy = [...META_DIRECTIVES, "script-src 'self' 'sha256-…'", "style-src 'self' 'sha256-…'"].join('; ');
const ownPolicy = `Content-Security-Policy: ${HEADER_POLICY}\n<meta http-equiv="Content-Security-Policy" content="${metaPolicy}">`;
const analyzeOwn = `/#${encodeState({ policy: ownPolicy, site: '', vendors: {} })}`;
---

<Base title="About" description="An independent, free tool to understand Content-Security-Policies. Your policy never leaves your browser.">
  <article class="wrap prose about">
    <h1>About</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      A free, independent tool to help everyone who works on a website, not only developers, understand its
      Content-Security-Policy and talk about it with confidence.
    </p>

    <h2>Your policy stays in your browser</h2>
    <p>
      Everything is computed on your device. The policy you paste is never sent to a server. Share links keep the policy after
      the <code>#</code> of the address, a part browsers never send to servers.
    </p>

    <h2>What we count</h2>
    <p>
      To know whether the site is useful, we count visits and a few actions: analysing a policy, trying the example, opening a
      share link, adding a tool, copying a report or the snippet. We keep daily totals, along with the name of the page, the tool
      or the report involved. No cookies, no third-party service, nothing that identifies you, and never your policy or your site
      address.
    </p>

    <h2>Where the information comes from</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Directive behaviour follows the <NewTabLink href="https://www.w3.org/TR/CSP3/" label="W3C Content Security Policy Level 3" /> specification.</li>
      <li>
        Security findings come from
        Google's <NewTabLink href="https://github.com/google/csp-evaluator" label="CSP Evaluator" /> library
        (Apache-2.0), the same checks as csp-evaluator.withgoogle.com.
      </li>
      <li>
        What each tool needs comes from the vendor's official documentation, linked on every entry with the date it was last
        checked. No vendor pays to be listed or influences the results.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Help keep the catalogue right</h2>
    <p>
      Vendors change their requirements. If an entry is outdated or a tool is
      missing, <NewTabLink href={`${REPO_URL}/issues`} label="open an issue" /> with a link to the official documentation.
    </p>

    <h2>This site's own policy</h2>
    <p>
      We follow our own advice. This site sends two policies: a header for what only a header can do (refusing to be embedded in
      other sites), and a <code>&lt;meta&gt;</code> tag with strict rules where scripts and styles are allowed by their exact
      fingerprint (hash).
    </p>
    <pre><code>{ownPolicy}</code></pre>
    <p><a class="button" href={analyzeOwn}>Analyse this site's policy</a></p>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .about {
    max-width: 52rem;
  }
  .about h2 {
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
  }
  .lead {
    font-size: var(--step-1);
  }
  pre {
    white-space: pre-wrap;
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }
  li {
    margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
  }
</style>
